\* Generated by formal/plx_formal.py from the ParallaXMux tables.
\* Do not edit by hand. Run: python3 formal/plx_formal.py emit
\*
\* Two TCP MUX streams: admission, half-close, local reset, task exit, and sibling isolation.
\*
\* Safety claims (states and steps that must be unreachable):
\*   MuxCapacityCountsBothHalves: a one-slot carrier never owns two unfinished supervisors
\*   MuxLocalEventsPreserveSibling: a frame, setup failure, or cancellation affects only its own stream
\*   MuxRejectedOpenAndCoverAreInert: duplicate/capacity Open rejection and Cover change neither stream
\*   MuxTeardownReleasesAllSlots: carrier teardown leaves no owned supervisor or target half
\*   MuxOwnership0: a live task and its slot remain paired until task exit
\*   MuxLiveHalfKeepsSlot0: one remaining relay direction still consumes capacity
\*   MuxFinIsHalfClose0: FIN removes upload routing while preserving the supervisor and both target halves
\*   MuxDataRequiresUploadRoute0: no new DATA is enqueued after upload routing is removed
\*   MuxResetKeepsSlotUntilExit0: requesting cancellation does not prematurely release its slot
\*   MuxOwnership1: a live task and its slot remain paired until task exit
\*   MuxLiveHalfKeepsSlot1: one remaining relay direction still consumes capacity
\*   MuxFinIsHalfClose1: FIN removes upload routing while preserving the supervisor and both target halves
\*   MuxDataRequiresUploadRoute1: no new DATA is enqueued after upload routing is removed
\*   MuxResetKeepsSlotUntilExit1: requesting cancellation does not prematurely release its slot

